{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775378585-XGYqnKvjXJlMRJ39dWLP","role":"assistant","created":1775378590,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, the JSON data seems to only have the period data, not the weekly data. Let me look at the txt file more carefully. Perhaps I need to examine a different part of the document or look for multiple tables on the same page.\n\nActually wait - in the original parsed text file, I saw weekly data for all four categories (short-term banking funds, brokerage balances, domestic securities, foreign securities). But maybe NET CAPITAL MOVEMENT only has period data, and the weekly net capital movement is calculated by summing the four components?\n\nLet me try that approach - sum up the four categories for Jan 18 and Jan 25.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_404fed7d060c4c1ab96f1af9","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Let me look at all four sections and extract weekly data for Latin America\n# The dates we need: Jan 18 (third Thursday) and Jan 25 (fourth Wednesday)\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_04_page_61.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\nimport re\n\n# Find each section and extract weekly data for Jan 18 and Jan 25 for Latin America\nsections = [\n    'MOVEMENT IN SHORT-TERM BANKING FUNDS',\n    'MOVEMENT IN BROKERAGE BALANCES', \n    'MOVEMENT IN TRANSACTIONS IN DOMESTIC SECURITIES',\n    'MOVEMENT IN TRANSACTIONS IN FOREIGN SECURITIES'\n]\n\nfor section_name in sections:\n    start = content.find(section_name)\n    if start != -1:\n        # Find end at next section\n        next_section_idx = float('inf')\n        for ns in sections:\n            idx = content.find(ns, start + 1)\n            if idx != -1 and idx < next_section_idx:\n                next_section_idx = idx\n        \n        section = content[start:next_section_idx]\n        \n        # Find rows for Jan 18 and Jan 25\n        for date in ['Jan. 18', 'Jan. 25']:\n            idx = section.find(date)\n            if idx != -1:\n                row = section[idx:idx+300]\n                # Extract the Latin America column (10th column)\n                cells = re.findall(r'<td>(.*?)</td>', row)\n                if len(cells) >= 10:\n                    latam = cells[9]\n                    print(f'{section_name} - {date}: Latin America = {latam}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
