{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775378608-z7wMmY23VigjG9n82M0b","role":"assistant","created":1775378617,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the columns clearly from the header. Looking at the row for Jan. 18:\n- Column 1 (index 0): Date = Jan. 18\n- Column 2 (index 1): United Kingdom = 4,399\n- Column 3 (index 2): France = 2,024\n- Column 4 (index 3): Germany = 1,509\n- Column 5 (index 4): Italy = 29\n- Column 6 (index 5): Netherlands = 3,015\n- Column 7 (index 6): Switzerland = -8,898\n- Column 8 (index 7): Other Europe = 6,165\n- Column 9 (index 8): Total Europe = 8,243\n- Column 10 (index 9): Canada = 11,807\n- Column 11 (index 10): Latin America = -468\n- Column 12 (index 11): Far East = 14,608\n- Column 13 (index 12): All other = -550\n- Column 14 (index 13): Grand total = 33,680\n\nSo for Jan 18, Latin America = -468 (in the SHORT-TERM BANKING FUNDS section)\n\nWait, but I'm seeing -468 in index 10. Let me verify:\n- cells[0] = Jan. 18\n- cells[1] = 4,399 (UK)\n- ...\n- cells[9] = 11,807 (Canada)\n- cells[10] = -468 (Latin America!)\n\nSo Latin America IS at index 10, not index 9!\n\nThe problem is my previous code was using index 9 which is Canada. Let me redo the extraction.\n\nWait, looking at the results from my earlier code:\n- 'MOVEMENT IN SHORT-TERM BANKING FUNDS - Jan. 18: Latin America = 11,807'\n\n\n- 'MOVEMENT IN SHORT-TERM BANKING FUNDS - Jan. 25: Latin America = -5,971'\n\nThese values are actually Canada, not Latin America. I need to use index 10 to get the correct column.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_0b525c62e43d41b4938bd78a","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_04_page_61.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\nimport re\n\n# Now let's extract properly - Latin America is column 11 (index 10)\n# Columns: Date, UK, France, Germany, Italy, Netherlands, Switzerland, Other Europe, Total Europe, Canada, Latin America, Far East, All other, Grand total\n\nsection_names = [\n    'MOVEMENT IN SHORT-TERM BANKING FUNDS:',\n    'MOVEMENT IN BROKERAGE BALANCES:', \n    'MOVEMENT IN TRANSACTIONS IN DOMESTIC SECURITIES:',\n    'MOVEMENT IN TRANSACTIONS IN FOREIGN SECURITIES:'\n]\n\nresults = {}\n\nfor section_name in section_names:\n    start = content.find(section_name)\n    if start != -1:\n        # Find end at next section\n        next_idx = float('inf')\n        for other in section_names:\n            if other != section_name:\n                idx = content.find(other, start + 1)\n                if idx != -1 and idx < next_idx:\n                    next_idx = idx\n        \n        section = content[start:next_idx]\n        \n        for date in ['Jan. 18', 'Jan. 25']:\n            idx = section.find(date)\n            if idx != -1:\n                row_start = section.rfind('<tr>', 0, idx)\n                row_end = section.find('</tr>', idx) + 5\n                row = section[row_start:row_end]\n                \n                # Extract cells - Latin America is at index 10\n                cells = re.findall(r'<td>(.*?)</td>', row)\n                if len(cells) >= 11:\n                    latam = cells[10]  # Latin America is column 11 (index 10)\n                    results[(section_name.replace(':', '').strip(), date)] = latam\n                    print(f'{section_name} - {date}: Latin America = {latam}')\n\nprint()\nprint('Summary of results:')\nfor k, v in results.items():\n    print(f'{k}: {v}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
